WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.032 --> 00:00:02.002
- He loved fitness ever since his dad

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:04.083
brought home a gym in the sixth grade.

00:00:04.083 --> 00:00:06.573
He's been an actor,
spokesperson, and model

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:09.348
for various commercials,
brands, and causes.

00:00:09.348 --> 00:00:11.881
He's one of the most recognized
and motivating people

00:00:11.881 --> 00:00:13.513
in the fitness industry.

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:14.539
He's Greg Plitt,

00:00:14.539 --> 00:00:18.039
and here are his top 10 rules for success.

00:00:20.063 --> 00:00:21.150
- How you see it,

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:23.085
whatever the truth is,

00:00:23.085 --> 00:00:25.059
your perception on how you see that truth

00:00:25.059 --> 00:00:26.900
outweighs it 10 to one,

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:30.600
so it's the motivation
and why you're doing it.

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:32.072
The journey of getting in shape,

00:00:32.072 --> 00:00:34.430
it's a long, long run. Right?

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:36.909
The person who's standing at
the end with their hand raised

00:00:36.909 --> 00:00:38.770
isn't the person with all the genetics.

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:40.555
It isn't the person
with the most potential.

00:00:40.555 --> 00:00:43.433
It's the person that has
the greatest perseverance,

00:00:43.433 --> 00:00:44.600
that's always willing to get up.

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:48.241
The difference between
a champion and a loser,

00:00:48.241 --> 00:00:49.476
you know, they both fail.

00:00:49.476 --> 00:00:52.365
It's just the loser allows
the failure to stand for life,

00:00:52.365 --> 00:00:54.376
where the champion, even though
he gets knocked on his ass,

00:00:54.376 --> 00:00:56.236
finds the intestinal
fortitude to stand back up,

00:00:56.236 --> 00:00:58.535
reface that endeavor
until it becomes his favor

00:00:58.535 --> 00:01:00.364
until he wins; that's the difference.

00:01:00.364 --> 00:01:02.286
Champions get back up and do it again.

00:01:02.286 --> 00:01:04.023
The difference between
someone that's successful here

00:01:04.023 --> 00:01:05.401
or someone's a spectator here

00:01:05.401 --> 00:01:07.546
is that a person's successful...

00:01:07.546 --> 00:01:09.422
They believe in themselves so much

00:01:09.422 --> 00:01:12.094
and their belief overrides
any crowd's disbelief.

00:01:12.094 --> 00:01:13.655
You have to be a student of the game.

00:01:13.655 --> 00:01:15.012
You have to know what nutrition is,

00:01:15.012 --> 00:01:17.216
what supplementation
is, why you're training.

00:01:17.216 --> 00:01:20.407
You can't be a blind squirrel
trying to find a nut everyday,

00:01:20.407 --> 00:01:22.219
meaning you have to
know what you're doing.

00:01:22.219 --> 00:01:23.299
In order for your body to change,

00:01:23.299 --> 00:01:25.277
it starts up top with the greatest muscle.

00:01:25.277 --> 00:01:26.621
Why you're doing what you're doing.

00:01:26.621 --> 00:01:27.554
If you're not a student of the game,

00:01:27.554 --> 00:01:29.741
then you don't understand
the ins and the outs

00:01:29.741 --> 00:01:31.913
of each daily operation.

00:01:31.913 --> 00:01:34.062
Success has nothing to do potential.

00:01:34.062 --> 00:01:36.088
It's all about the
perseverance of somebody.

00:01:36.088 --> 00:01:38.208
That will override any endeavor.

00:01:38.208 --> 00:01:39.505
If you throw (beep) against the wall,

00:01:39.505 --> 00:01:41.263
eventually something will stick.

00:01:41.263 --> 00:01:42.558
You guys that have this potential,

00:01:42.558 --> 00:01:43.913
don't have this potential...

00:01:43.913 --> 00:01:45.740
You know, that (beep) dies.

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:47.548
What continues to last forever

00:01:47.548 --> 00:01:49.717
is a perseverance to always show up.

00:01:49.717 --> 00:01:50.759
That's what champions do.

00:01:50.759 --> 00:01:53.607
Every single champion is the
same as every ordinary person.

00:01:53.607 --> 00:01:55.210
The only differential is that they show up

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:56.700
to the event every single day.

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:58.807
They see failure as a learning curve.

00:01:58.807 --> 00:02:00.140
They welcome failure.

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:03.510
You learn more from failure
than you ever will from success.

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:05.428
So showing up and getting
knocked on your ass,

00:02:05.428 --> 00:02:07.093
finding the intestinal
fortitude, stand back up

00:02:07.093 --> 00:02:09.034
and reface that endeavor,

00:02:09.034 --> 00:02:12.212
is going to be the overriding
factor that makes a difference.

00:02:12.212 --> 00:02:13.807
How do you know when
you're doing those things?

00:02:13.807 --> 00:02:15.907
The small things in
life add up to those big

00:02:15.907 --> 00:02:16.876
monumental things.

00:02:16.876 --> 00:02:17.709
And when I say the small things,

00:02:17.709 --> 00:02:19.030
it's a character building block.

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:22.078
That your name means something,
you hold value to your name.

00:02:22.078 --> 00:02:23.232
If you drop trash on the ground,

00:02:23.232 --> 00:02:24.876
you pick it up 'cause
that's your responsibility.

00:02:24.876 --> 00:02:26.265
You hold value to yourself.

00:02:26.265 --> 00:02:28.026
When you shake someone's
hand, you look them in the eye

00:02:28.026 --> 00:02:29.227
and give them a firm handshake

00:02:29.227 --> 00:02:31.234
'cause you're here for a purpose.

00:02:31.234 --> 00:02:33.316
Everything you do, you do
to the best of your ability.

00:02:33.316 --> 00:02:34.864
Doesn't matter what you're doing,

00:02:34.864 --> 00:02:36.060
it's the fact that you're doing it.

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:38.053
So therefore it means something to you.

00:02:38.053 --> 00:02:39.540
That's going to build the legacy

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:42.214
'cause the title out
there doesn't mean (beep).

00:02:42.214 --> 00:02:43.607
You win the title, fine.

00:02:43.607 --> 00:02:45.516
That title will not get you another title.

00:02:45.516 --> 00:02:48.072
What you're trying to build is a legacy.

00:02:48.072 --> 00:02:49.501
Footprints behind you,

00:02:49.501 --> 00:02:51.671
they're left for motivation
for someone else to follow.

00:02:51.671 --> 00:02:54.419
Legacy is built daily
through the character,

00:02:54.419 --> 00:02:57.976
the willpower, the code of
conduct within somebody.

00:02:57.976 --> 00:02:59.067
And that's the perseverance.

00:02:59.067 --> 00:03:01.076
Showing up every single day.

00:03:01.076 --> 00:03:02.547
That will always achieve your goal.

00:03:02.547 --> 00:03:04.199
It doesn't matter what you're born with.

00:03:04.199 --> 00:03:06.117
It doesn't matter your potential,

00:03:06.117 --> 00:03:07.822
the silver spoon or money you have.

00:03:07.822 --> 00:03:10.172
All of that can be
attained if you show up,

00:03:10.172 --> 00:03:14.267
and you're willing to
risk failure for success.

00:03:14.267 --> 00:03:17.229
I went through the life:
the military and sports.

00:03:17.229 --> 00:03:19.087
I always use the gym for some means.

00:03:19.087 --> 00:03:20.968
It was never about fitness modeling.

00:03:20.968 --> 00:03:22.664
I just had a passion for working out.

00:03:22.664 --> 00:03:24.957
Every time I hit struggles
or I was stressed out,

00:03:24.957 --> 00:03:27.871
I went to the gym to find solidity there,

00:03:27.871 --> 00:03:29.058
to work through any kind of stresses.

00:03:29.058 --> 00:03:31.008
So, naturally I got in shape,

00:03:31.008 --> 00:03:32.755
but it wasn't for fitness modeling,

00:03:32.755 --> 00:03:35.011
it was for military and sports.

00:03:35.011 --> 00:03:36.752
And then, later on down the road,

00:03:36.752 --> 00:03:38.200
an agency saw me, and said,

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:39.205
hey, you should take some pictures.

00:03:39.205 --> 00:03:40.271
I'm like, I'll try it.

00:03:40.271 --> 00:03:41.756
And that's how this was born.

00:03:41.756 --> 00:03:42.815
It wasn't this starting.

00:03:42.815 --> 00:03:44.670
I didn't start out, set out for this.

00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:47.216
It just ended up coming to a passion

00:03:47.216 --> 00:03:49.169
and the love of the gym.

00:03:49.169 --> 00:03:51.796
I could teach you whatever,
but when you go out there,

00:03:51.796 --> 00:03:54.675
and you try it yourself, and
you fall flat on your face.

00:03:54.675 --> 00:03:56.223
That's where you learn it the most.

00:03:56.223 --> 00:03:57.141
Because the next time when you fall,

00:03:57.141 --> 00:03:58.718
you got to learn to catch
yourself, and that's a lesson

00:03:58.718 --> 00:03:59.851
you never forget.

00:03:59.851 --> 00:04:01.549
So everyone wants a war game.

00:04:01.549 --> 00:04:03.145
Everyone wants to sit back, and what ifs,

00:04:03.145 --> 00:04:04.403
and before they start their journey,

00:04:04.403 --> 00:04:06.648
they want to plan it out,
war game, and war game.

00:04:06.648 --> 00:04:07.886
Just get going, man.

00:04:07.886 --> 00:04:09.884
Get going. You'll learn it along the way.

00:04:09.884 --> 00:04:11.347
And some people want
to be a fitness model,

00:04:11.347 --> 00:04:13.144
so they'll try to figure
out all fitness model stuff

00:04:13.144 --> 00:04:14.104
to be a fitness model.

00:04:14.104 --> 00:04:16.011
But you just fall in
love with the passion.

00:04:16.011 --> 00:04:17.489
I know a lot of people
that started out to be

00:04:17.489 --> 00:04:19.721
a fitness model, but that
wasn't the real passion.

00:04:19.721 --> 00:04:21.288
But they didn't know it
until they started it,

00:04:21.288 --> 00:04:23.959
and now the photographer,
the editor, or an actor

00:04:23.959 --> 00:04:25.901
coming up to LA, that
now is a great producer

00:04:25.901 --> 00:04:28.299
or director; you don't
know what the field is.

00:04:28.299 --> 00:04:30.802
Just get going and figure it out.

00:04:30.802 --> 00:04:32.743
And then the truth will surface.

00:04:32.743 --> 00:04:34.849
Action causes reaction, you know.

00:04:34.849 --> 00:04:37.948
If you stand still in a sedative state,

00:04:37.948 --> 00:04:40.355
if you're a pond and it's sedative,

00:04:40.355 --> 00:04:42.898
what grows in there is algae; mosquitoes.

00:04:42.898 --> 00:04:43.837
No one wants that.

00:04:43.837 --> 00:04:46.495
But if you have a current,
a fountain or something

00:04:46.495 --> 00:04:47.328
it's like an oasis.

00:04:47.328 --> 00:04:48.844
People want to come and look at it.

00:04:48.844 --> 00:04:50.423
Your life has to be moving the same way.

00:04:50.423 --> 00:04:51.516
When you guys are sitting on the couch,

00:04:51.516 --> 00:04:52.658
or wherever you're watching this,

00:04:52.658 --> 00:04:54.272
- Yeah
- to take that first step

00:04:54.272 --> 00:04:55.433
- Yep
- towards greatness

00:04:55.433 --> 00:04:56.266
is very hard.

00:04:56.266 --> 00:04:57.343
That's the hardest step of everything,

00:04:57.343 --> 00:04:58.492
is that first step, right.

00:04:58.492 --> 00:04:59.325
- Yep.
- That first step

00:04:59.325 --> 00:05:00.830
towards greatness is hard.

00:05:00.830 --> 00:05:02.249
- Yeah.
- But what's a lot harder,

00:05:02.249 --> 00:05:04.008
- Yeah.
- is when time expires

00:05:04.008 --> 00:05:04.940
in life, you look back
- Yeah, yeah.

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:07.611
- on your life, knowing
you could have been great.

00:05:07.611 --> 00:05:08.943
That's something you
can't control anymore,

00:05:08.943 --> 00:05:09.998
because time has run out.

00:05:09.998 --> 00:05:11.684
I have the greatest job in the world.

00:05:11.684 --> 00:05:14.721
It's a job where I get
to put out what I do,

00:05:14.721 --> 00:05:16.971
what I love to do, and
help to inspire people

00:05:16.971 --> 00:05:19.127
to do what they love, and achieve things.

00:05:19.127 --> 00:05:22.403
I come to these expos, and
people wait three hours,

00:05:22.403 --> 00:05:25.498
or drive 10 hours, or a plane,
and they wait in these lines,

00:05:25.498 --> 00:05:26.430
and they come up to me and they say,

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:27.793
thank you for everything you're doing,

00:05:27.793 --> 00:05:28.819
you've really saved my life.

00:05:28.819 --> 00:05:31.137
You're a huge motivation,
a huge difference.

00:05:31.137 --> 00:05:34.777
And they don't understand
how much that means to me.

00:05:34.777 --> 00:05:36.940
Because that's the greatest thing in life.

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:39.002
That's the legacy that
you actually do something

00:05:39.002 --> 00:05:40.884
to lead an impact towards others.

00:05:40.884 --> 00:05:42.671
And there's no greater honor than that.

00:05:42.671 --> 00:05:44.095
It's not until I come here
and someone takes time

00:05:44.095 --> 00:05:48.264
out of their day, that
gives value to what I do.

00:05:48.264 --> 00:05:50.496
They use it to transform
themselves, to get belief

00:05:50.496 --> 00:05:52.351
in themselves, to change
their life, to become

00:05:52.351 --> 00:05:54.004
the person they've always wanted to be.

00:05:54.004 --> 00:05:55.055
And they come and they share that,

00:05:55.055 --> 00:05:55.888
and they thank me for that.

00:05:55.888 --> 00:05:58.251
But the thing is, it's
their sweat on their shirt.

00:05:58.251 --> 00:05:59.438
Not mine.

00:05:59.438 --> 00:06:01.475
I just help them believe in themselves.

00:06:01.475 --> 00:06:04.512
And to have a small
impact in the betterment

00:06:04.512 --> 00:06:07.140
of their life, that
just humbles me so much.

00:06:07.140 --> 00:06:09.090
And so that's why I
think I have the greatest

00:06:09.090 --> 00:06:10.100
job in the world.

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:12.303
Because, the return of investment.

00:06:12.303 --> 00:06:17.071
It's not a monetary value,
but it's a value that,

00:06:17.071 --> 00:06:18.533
that builds legacy.

00:06:18.533 --> 00:06:20.738
It's not the dog in
the fight that matters,

00:06:20.738 --> 00:06:22.649
it's the fight in the dog that matters.

00:06:22.649 --> 00:06:23.680
Same with you.

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:25.390
It's not your genetics, or your potential,

00:06:25.390 --> 00:06:27.624
it's how bad do you want it.

00:06:27.624 --> 00:06:30.594
Going to the gym is not
about checking the box,

00:06:30.594 --> 00:06:32.150
you know, paid my dues today.

00:06:32.150 --> 00:06:35.875
I go in there and I find,
it's self discovery.

00:06:35.875 --> 00:06:37.766
It's like there's something about that

00:06:37.766 --> 00:06:42.527
eighth rep, when you can't
do it; of who you are.

00:06:42.527 --> 00:06:44.131
When you're pushing it,
trying to get it up,

00:06:44.131 --> 00:06:46.019
and, do we just quit?

00:06:46.019 --> 00:06:47.447
Do we just rack it?

00:06:47.447 --> 00:06:49.507
Or, do we rack it, drop
the weight, and keep going

00:06:49.507 --> 00:06:51.448
for the burn, or do we
get someone to spot us?

00:06:51.448 --> 00:06:52.956
Who are we in that adversity?

00:06:52.956 --> 00:06:54.352
Do we push past it?

00:06:54.352 --> 00:06:56.869
Do we try to get more out
of it, or do we settle?

00:06:56.869 --> 00:06:59.048
Do we say words like, good enough?

00:06:59.048 --> 00:07:00.696
And if you do say, good
enough, you're in trouble

00:07:00.696 --> 00:07:03.664
because you don't know if
you have enough, until later.

00:07:03.664 --> 00:07:06.000
I always say if you never
use terms like, good enough,

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:07.460
tomorrow you'll always have enough.

00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:09.173
So, I like to leave it
all there when I work out,

00:07:09.173 --> 00:07:12.119
and no matter what happens later in life,

00:07:12.119 --> 00:07:15.569
I know it's not because of
my shortcomings done today.

00:07:15.569 --> 00:07:18.266
Those three reps I could have
done; is that the difference

00:07:18.266 --> 00:07:19.488
of me being successful later?

00:07:19.488 --> 00:07:20.356
I don't know.

00:07:20.356 --> 00:07:21.947
That's why I do those
three reps, so I never

00:07:21.947 --> 00:07:22.988
have to wonder what if.

00:07:22.988 --> 00:07:23.821
How do you stay motivated?

00:07:23.821 --> 00:07:24.984
Guys, you want to get a partner.

00:07:24.984 --> 00:07:26.572
Champions come in pairs of two cause they

00:07:26.572 --> 00:07:28.223
bound themselves in perfection.

00:07:28.223 --> 00:07:31.062
A partner is not only an asset to you

00:07:31.062 --> 00:07:32.921
on the physical side,
but also the mental side,

00:07:32.921 --> 00:07:34.608
meaning when you guys
are coming home from work

00:07:34.608 --> 00:07:36.472
or something, when maybe
the wife is just (beep)

00:07:36.472 --> 00:07:38.547
yelling at you too much,
and it's driving you

00:07:38.547 --> 00:07:40.428
into a migraine, or the kids are just...

00:07:40.428 --> 00:07:41.627
You know, it's one of
those days, you know,

00:07:41.627 --> 00:07:43.571
the boss is on you
(beep) seems like (beep).

00:07:43.571 --> 00:07:45.952
I just need to go to the bar or something.

00:07:45.952 --> 00:07:47.478
Well, if you have a
partner, your partner's

00:07:47.478 --> 00:07:48.311
going to be calling you,

00:07:48.311 --> 00:07:49.224
hey man, ready to hit the gym?

00:07:49.224 --> 00:07:50.493
You're like, dude, man,
I just had a long day and

00:07:50.493 --> 00:07:51.687
everything else; I'm
just not feeling it, man,

00:07:51.687 --> 00:07:53.473
not going to the gym.

00:07:53.473 --> 00:07:56.208
And so, you let him down.

00:07:56.208 --> 00:07:59.569
Now, we can all fool ourselves,
and bury the real truth

00:07:59.569 --> 00:08:03.152
inside of us of why
we're not going, right.

00:08:04.038 --> 00:08:06.994
And kid ourselves for
whatever (beep) reasons,

00:08:06.994 --> 00:08:09.748
or these excuses that mean
nothing, but we give them value,

00:08:09.748 --> 00:08:12.549
we give them weight, to make us not go,

00:08:12.549 --> 00:08:14.904
so we can fail on our own account.

00:08:14.904 --> 00:08:17.083
But you got to be a
really low (beep, beep),

00:08:17.083 --> 00:08:20.203
to fail on somebody that's relying on you.

00:08:20.203 --> 00:08:22.026
Very few people would do that.

00:08:22.026 --> 00:08:23.826
When you make a commitment;
a verbal, written commitment

00:08:23.826 --> 00:08:26.987
to somebody, your word should
mean something to them.

00:08:26.987 --> 00:08:28.739
When they call you up
and say, hey, let's go,

00:08:28.739 --> 00:08:29.942
and you're like, dude,
man, I'm not into it, man,

00:08:29.942 --> 00:08:31.661
not into it.

00:08:31.661 --> 00:08:33.751
Wow, so you're not into it;
not like it affects you,

00:08:33.751 --> 00:08:35.180
but also affects someone else's day.

00:08:35.180 --> 00:08:37.003
No, what's going to happen is
that guy's going to pull you

00:08:37.003 --> 00:08:39.321
into the gym, drag your
(beep) through the workout,

00:08:39.321 --> 00:08:40.772
even though you didn't want to.

00:08:40.772 --> 00:08:42.808
And by expending that
energy in a tired state,

00:08:42.808 --> 00:08:44.222
you can come out of the
gym with a sense of pride

00:08:44.222 --> 00:08:46.296
and relief, or you know,
morphed out energy,

00:08:46.296 --> 00:08:47.546
like, wow, man.

00:08:48.426 --> 00:08:49.482
You know, that felt good.

00:08:49.482 --> 00:08:51.199
Now you're going to go
back into your problems

00:08:51.199 --> 00:08:52.139
that you didn't want to go to the gym

00:08:52.139 --> 00:08:53.304
'cause they're overwhelming, and you can

00:08:53.304 --> 00:08:54.430
look at 'em differently.

